    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for containerd",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for containerd fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-39882: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp: Memory exhaustion via uncapped HTTP\n  response body reading (bsc#1274214).\n- CVE-2026-47262: Denial of Service (DoS) condition via a maliciously crafted image (bsc#1268441).\n- CVE-2026-53488: CRI plugin propagates labels from an image config to a container without validation (bsc#1268430).\n- CVE-2026-53493: a crafted OCI index graph can force very high CPU/memory usage during PullImage (before container\n  start), causing long ContainerCreating stalls and, at larger sizes, node/runtime instability (bsc#1282669).\n- CVE-2026-53495: CRI ExecSync Goroutine Leak Leads to Node-Level Denial of Service (bsc#1280007).\n- CVE-2026-95838: github.com/containerd/containerd: processing of certain image layers causes superlinear time\n  complexity in unpack handler and can lead to DoS (bsc#1285124).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLE-Micro-6.1-765",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
